{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.\n\nInspected: Read complete rectangle/SheetData definitions, torus and sheet coordinates, classical PDE comparison class, effective evaluation and bounds, and full sheet_theorem; compared audited sheet theorem.","content_sha256":"sha256:bb585971d5a335af20aa326a0cc11a04446fa699b1669b703857ae7ef8ee19d4","fingerprint":"sha256:365bd161e2770dfc665006d1131bd618bb5c35268319e4401735b7f4bc7d45ff","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:25fcf5559472bfc5c5696a14098489382dc82c5915a0c8e7ca1221a8ce2b6593","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Solenoidal.sheet_theorem"],"explanation":"The formal SheetData gives separately separated rational source and target rectangles in [2,3]^2 and positive diagonal maps onto their targets, without imposing source-target separation or area preservation. At positive computable viscosity its theorem realizes their sheet maps at height two on the side-ten torus by effective smooth mean-zero solenoidal forcing, one-periodic from zero. It also matches pressure zero, classical uniqueness, velocity collars at integer times, zero self-advection, bounded mixed derivatives and the zero-program case.","fingerprint":"sha256:a78ffe21379b78b622bf980428a919a91d8343d4e5942f2061458930dacc4ac9","limitations":"This is a finite sheet-program realization; it does not itself assert a halting equivalence or a volume-preserving map of three-dimensional solid boxes.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Geometric-Programs-for-Solenoidal-Forcing-September-27-2026#sv:sheet-theorem","statement_sha256":"sha256:379711dd4d71453d06f16fe1959ee78f35d7eefbbe73d6de070418deccdcbd2a"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SolenoidalSheetPrograms.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Geometric-Programs-for-Solenoidal-Forcing-September-27-2026/build/introduction.tex#L75"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:SolenoidalSheetPrograms","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.Solenoidal.sheet_theorem","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/SolenoidalSheetPrograms.lean","line":175,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"25fcf5559472bfc5c5696a14098489382dc82c5915a0c8e7ca1221a8ce2b6593","statement_sha256":"sha256:a3132951e07fefd0be7ff8fe485ca494135f161e5508ed41ed06573d9642bdbc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SolenoidalSheetPrograms.lean#L175"},"text":"theorem sheet_theorem {N : ℕ} (D : SheetData N) (ν : ℝ)\n    (hν : 0 < ν) (hνcomp : ComputableReal ν) :\n    ∃ f u : Field, ∃ X : ℝ → Space → Space,\n      SpatiallyPeriodic f ∧ SpatiallyPeriodic u ∧\n      Smooth f ∧ Smooth u ∧ Effective f ∧\n      MeanZero f ∧ DivergenceFree f ∧ OnePeriodic f ∧\n      ClassicalSolution ν f u (fun _ _ => 0) ∧\n      (∀ v : Field, ∀ p : Pressure, ClassicalSolution ν f v p →\n        ∀ t, 0 ≤ t → ∀ x, v t x = u t x ∧ p t x = 0) ∧\n      MaterialFlow u X ∧\n      (∀ i : Fin N, ∀ y ∈ (D.source i).carrier,\n        toTorus (X 1 (sheet y)) =\n          toTorus (sheet (diagonalMap (D.source i) (D.target i) (D.ratio i) y))) ∧\n      IntegerCollars u ∧ (∀ t x, advection u t x = 0) ∧\n      EffectiveBounds f ∧ EffectiveBounds u ∧\n      (N = 0 → f = 0 ∧ u = 0)"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"l:SolenoidalSheetPrograms","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f:376":{"alternatives":["pair:cef86d51ebc3a53dce2a7ec4","pair:3cf7839c4aa7509f301d4122","pair:7d69002525b43d13b91dbf5e","pair:db5894fd3300272b56d23aed","pair:4c257b6733f5e4d5961a48e0"],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"content_sha256":"sha256:bb585971d5a335af20aa326a0cc11a04446fa699b1669b703857ae7ef8ee19d4","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/2c26c113b43754d3f3d13d9f.json","pointer":"/contributions/0"},"provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"review_state":"unreviewed","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Solenoidal.sheet_theorem"],"limitations":"This is a finite sheet-program realization; it does not itself assert a halting equivalence or a volume-preserving map of three-dimensional solid boxes.","relation":"same-claim","target":"r:Geometric-Programs-for-Sole